In article <1993Apr2.120712.2297@gnv.ifas.ufl.edu> afc@gnv.ifas.ufl.edu writes:
>Playing 3.11 on a PC:

Um, that's 3.1.1.

>My solution was to put the Amulet into my bag of holding.  Of course 
>the development team thought of that, and the bag can't contain the Amulet.
>But what if the Amulet was inside of something else?  That does work, and
>I was able to go up the stairs normally.  If I had really believed that
>this was working I would have just level teleported to level 1.

Spoiler...


>The only trick is figuring out how to get the Amulet inside of something,
>and then knowing how to get it back out.

Um, hand it to some monster, bop said monster with a cockatrice
corpse, and carry the resulting statue up to the first level.
Crack open the statue with a pickaxe when you get up to the top.

Heck, just hit the High Priest with the cockatrice corpse directly.
You could polymorph into a cockatrice or bring in a pet, too.  Wishing
for a blessed figurine of a cockatrice might work, but I think pets
won't attack monsters of higher level.  A ring of conflict would talk
rover into it, though.

Of course, you're going to end up with a lot of extra weight this
way.  A bag of holding would help.  You should be able to level
teleport directly at this point and save a _lot_ of time.

Interesting idea....  The dev team should most certainly fix this
particular problem.  Giving the holder of the Amulet stone resistance
would do the trick.

